messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Role: You coordinate clarification questions proposed by two independent questioning agents.
Task: Select and refine a complementary question set for workflow reconstruction and automation assessment.
Judge each candidate using the initial description: its relevance, the uncertainty it addresses,
the value of obtaining its answer, its likely burden on the respondent, and overlap with other candidates.
Preserve useful diverse perspectives. Do not assume any source is more authoritative.
Avoid redundant questions and bundles of unrelated information needs. You may select, rephrase,
or merge overlapping candidate questions, but cannot introduce an unrelated question.
You do not have the reference answers. Do not guess them or assume which facts an expert knows.
Candidate questions:
[
  {
    "candidate_id": "C1",
    "question": "What event or condition triggers the start of a specification document review — for example, is it a new document version being published, a change request being submitted, or a scheduled review date being reached?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C2",
    "question": "Is the specification document review performed by a single engineer working alone, or does it involve multiple reviewers whose findings must be consolidated before the review is considered complete?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C3",
    "question": "How does the engineer identify which parts of the document need to be reviewed — for instance, do they use a diff against a previous version, a checklist of expected features, or do they review the entire document each time?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C4",
    "question": "In what format and location is the specification document stored when it enters the review step — for example, a version-controlled repository, a shared editing platform, or a static file attachment?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C5",
    "question": "Can you walk me through the specific steps the engineer performs during the review itself — for example, what do they check first, what tools or references do they use, and in what order do activities typically occur?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C6",
    "question": "What artifact does the engineer produce to record review findings, and where does that artifact go after the review — for instance, inline annotations, a structured report, or issues logged in a tracking tool?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C7",
    "question": "When the engineer finds an issue such as a typo or a missing detail, what happens next — who is responsible for making the correction, how is the issue recorded, and does the document come back to the engineer for re-review?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C8",
    "question": "What specific criteria or checklist does the engineer use to decide whether a feature is correctly reflected in the document, and what are the possible outcomes of that judgment (e.g., approved, needs minor edits, needs major revision)?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C9",
    "question": "Is the review performed by a single engineer acting alone, or are there other roles involved — such as a document author, a second reviewer, or an approver — and if so, how does the work pass between them?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C10",
    "question": "What happens when the engineer discovers a significant gap or blocking issue during the review — for example, is the document sent back to the author, escalated to a lead, or does the review process pause until the issue is resolved?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C11",
    "question": "What marks the review as officially complete — for example, is there a formal sign-off, a status update in a tracking system, a review report that is produced, or something else?"
  },
  {
    "candidate_id": "C12",
    "question": "What triggers a new review instance — for example, a specific event such as a feature branch merge or a release milestone — and roughly how often does this review occur?"
  }
]
Return JSON with this shape:
{"missing_information": [{"category": "short label", "gap": "missing information", "why_it_matters": "reason"}],
"clarification_questions": [{"id": "Q1", "question": "final expert-facing question", "targets": ["short label"],
"source_ids": ["C1"], "selection_reason": "brief reason for including this question"}]}
Return exactly 6 questions with unique IDs Q1 through Q6.
Each question must have one main information need. Cite at least one valid candidate ID in source_ids.
Do not use any candidate ID for more than one final question.

